---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Splitwise Limits & Alternatives — Roommate";
const description = "Splitwise now restricts free users to 3 expenses per day with 10-second wait timers. Here are the best free alternatives for flatmates in 2026.";
const keywords = "splitwise limits 2026, splitwise daily limit, splitwise review 2026, best free splitwise alternative, why splitwise has wait timer";

const articleSchema = {
  headline: title,
  description: description,
  datePublished: "2026-11-15T08:00:00Z",
  authorName: "Umesh Jaiswal"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  ogType="article"
  publishDate="2026-11-15T08:00:00Z"
  articleSchema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com" },
    { name: "Blog", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog" },
    { name: "Splitwise 2026 Review", url: "https://roommatesexpensemanager.com/blog/splitwise-limits-and-best-free-alternatives-2026" }
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 space-y-10 text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-[#f5f5f7] text-[16px] sm:text-[17px] leading-relaxed transition-colors duration-200">
    <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 pb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-[#86868b] font-medium">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00966d]/10 dark:bg-[#00e599]/15 text-[#00966d] dark:text-[#00e599] font-semibold">App Comparisons</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>November 15, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="apple-hero-display text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Splitwise Limitations in 2026: Why You Need a Dedicated Free Alternative
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[18px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
        From beloved student utility to frustrating paywalled product: an honest examination of the changes driving flatmates away from Splitwise.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">What Changed in Splitwise</h2>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        For nearly a decade, Splitwise was the default answer whenever roommates, travel buddies, or couples asked: <em>"How should we split bills?"</em>
      </p>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        However, starting in late 2023 and intensifying throughout 2025 and 2026, Splitwise introduced severe restrictions on free users that disrupted basic day-to-day usability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">The 3 Major Friction Points</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-[22px] bg-[#f5f5f7] dark:bg-[#1d1d1f] border border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 text-base">1. The 3 Expenses Per Day Restriction</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
            In an active flat with 3 roommates, you easily log morning coffee/milk, afternoon groceries, evening takeaway, and an electric bill on the same day. Capping entries at 3 turns a utility tool into a blocker.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-[22px] bg-[#f5f5f7] dark:bg-[#1d1d1f] border border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 text-base">2. The 10-Second Wait Screen</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
            To force free users to upgrade, the app forces an artificial 10-second countdown before you can tap "Save". When you are in a rush at a payment terminal, waiting 10 seconds is intolerable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-[22px] bg-[#f5f5f7] dark:bg-[#1d1d1f] border border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 text-base">3. Pushy Pro Up-sells ($39.99/year)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] leading-relaxed">
            For college students and young professionals sharing a flat, spending ₹3,000+ per year just to log shared rent and groceries is completely impractical.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="apple-display-lg text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">Why Roommate is Built Different</h2>
      <p class="text-[#1d1d1f]/90 dark:text-[#f5f5f7]/90 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Roommate</strong> was engineered to be what bill-splitting was always supposed to be: lightweight, fast, and completely free.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-[#86868b] dark:text-[#a1a1a6] pl-2 text-[15px]">
        <li><strong>No Daily Limits:</strong> Log 50 expenses a day without restriction.</li>
        <li><strong>No Wait Timers:</strong> Saves instantly in milliseconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile PIN Login:</strong> No passwords or SMS OTP friction.</li>
        <li><strong>Live Excel View:</strong> Real-time matrix view of the whole month.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="pt-8 border-t border-black/8 dark:border-white/10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <p class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-[#1d1d1f] dark:text-white">Switch to Roommate today.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#86868b]">100% free forever, zero daily caps, zero countdown timers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/splitwise-alternative" class="apple-btn-primary">
          Compare vs Splitwise
        </a>
        <a href="/blog" class="apple-btn-secondary">
          <span>All Guides</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
